19	 * to E.164, so the hash is stable for a given owner.
20	 *
21	 * <p>When the computed code collides with an existing owner's {@code customerCode}, it is
22	 * de-duplicated by appending {@code -<n>} with the smallest {@code n} of 2 or more that
23	 * makes it unique (e.g. {@code NSW-A1B2C3D4-2}), so distinct owners always receive
24	 * distinct customer codes.
25	 */
